      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "declaration-template"
        },
        "title": "3. Give it a face",
        "body": "A graph presents itself through a Surface: a chain of Views, richest first, ending in a Glyph. Drag from the surface handle on the Declaration to make the first View. Drag from that View's next-view handle to add a smaller one. Add a Glyph last and connect it, so the chain ends in a mark that still reads at a tiny size.\n\nOne View is enough to begin. Twilite shows the richest View that fits the room it has, and the Glyph when there is almost none. This page is exactly that: a page, a summary card, an icon, then a glyph.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
