        "title": "6. Lay it out",
        "body": "Put each kind of node in its own place so the graph reads at a glance. The Declaration goes top left. Import bridges run down the left side. Export bridges take the top half of the right side and portals the bottom half. Views run along the bottom, and everything else stays inside that boundary.\n\nLook at this graph: that is where everything is. An empty region is fine. The layout is about where things sit, not about filling every corner.",
